<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Fixed acidity in wine refers to the non-volatile acids present, such as tartaric, malic, citric, and succinic acids, which contribute to the wine's tartness and freshness. It is measured in grams per liter \(g/L\) or milliequivalents per liter \(meq/L\).)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
