/ActualText (Volatile acidity \(VA\) in wine refers to the presence of volatile organic acids, primarily acetic acid, that can be detected by their aroma. High levels can indicate spoilage or fermentation issues, and VA can be measured by titration.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
