266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Residual sugar \(RS\) in wine refers to the natural sugars that remain after fermentation. It can come from grapes or be added, and its level can vary from dry to sweet. Residual sugar affects taste, mouthfeel, and sweetness, measured in g/L or as a percentage of the wine's total volume.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
