/ActualText (Each value in this vector indicates the degree of linear relationship between "quality" and a specific variable. When interpreting these correlation coefficients with values close to 1 or -1 indicate a strong correlation between the variables. A positive value suggests that as "quality" increases, the associated variable also tends to increase, while a negative value suggests an inverse relationship. Values close to 0 suggest a weak or negligible correlation between "quality" and the variable.  These color and size gradients highlight strong correlations.  For instance, we know citric acid has little to no significant relationship to the quality of wine as the correlogram shows a value of nearly 0.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
